Notebook[{
Cell["Phase 0 : Intra-Plane Elastic Translation-Addition Operator", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"e4ed297a-2432-4ee6-8933-8f0569f0d02b"],

Cell["\<\
Cruzan/Stein vector-spherical-wave translation for horizontal (Delta z = 0) \
separations. Built on a single scalar separation matrix beta^c(d) at k_P and \
k_S, dressed by the translation-commuting operators L=(1/k)grad, M=curl((r-c) \
.), N=(1/k)curl. Self-verifying: scalar addition theorem (vs projection \
integral and field reconstruction), vector field reconstruction (L, M, N), \
and reciprocity. Executable twin: IntraPlaneTranslation.wl. Independently \
validated against Python in \
cubic_scattering/tests/test_intraplane_translation.py.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40510432-57ea-43b4-91f6-e60a6e0ae068"],

Cell["\<\
IntraPlaneTranslation.wl  --  Phase 0 of the Intra-Plane Foldy-Lax program:
   the elastic vector-spherical-wave translation-addition operator \
(Cruzan/Stein).

   Outgoing L/M/N multipoles centred at A  ->  regular L/M/N multipoles \
centred at B,
   for a horizontal (Delta z = 0) separation.  The vector operator is built \
on a
   single SCALAR separation matrix beta^c_{nm,nu mu}(d) at c = P (k_P) and c \
= S (k_S),
   dressed by the fixed operators  L=(1/k)grad,  M=curl((r-c) .),  \
N=(1/k)curl  (plain Hansen).

   Conventions (inherited verbatim from CartesianT0.wl, reciprocity-verified \
1e-18):
     time e^{+i w t}; outgoing h_n^(1); orthonormal SphericalHarmonicY.
     Direction triples are (x,y,z) with z = polar axis = 3rd component
     (ang[d] reads d[[3]] as the polar component).  The VSH polar axis is \
aligned
     with the physical depth z, so an intra-plane separation is d = (d_x, \
d_y, 0).

   TDD: each accept-criterion is a numeric residual printed at the bottom \
with PASS/FAIL.
   Status VERIFIED: scalar separation matrix vs independent projection \
integral 2.8e-11 and
   field reconstruction 6.7e-11; vector L/M/N reconstruction PASS (L 6.7e-9, \
M 9.9e-10,
   N 6.0e-8) with the naive no-cross-term M shown to FAIL; reciprocity exact \
at k_P and k_S.
   Cross-validated in Python: \
cubic_scattering/tests/test_intraplane_translation.py.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e5eb733f-08c4-4cf8-b649-d622e37b5123"],

Cell["\<\
(* ---- spherical Bessel / Hankel (matching CartesianT0.wl) ---- *)
sj[n_, x_] := SphericalBesselJ[n, x];
sh[n_, x_] := SphericalBesselJ[n, x] + I SphericalBesselY[n, x];
zfn[n_, x_, \"j\"] := sj[n, x];
zfn[n_, x_, \"h\"] := sh[n, x];

(* ---- direction -> (theta, phi); copied verbatim from CartesianT0.wl ---- \
*)
ang[d_] := {ArcCos[d[[3]]/Sqrt[d . d]], ArcTan[d[[1]], d[[2]]]};
Yfun[n_, m_, d_] := SphericalHarmonicY[n, m, ang[d][[1]], ang[d][[2]]];

(* ---- scalar Helmholtz multipole field, centred at c, evaluated at field \
point r ---- *)
(* t = \"j\" regular (j_n) or \"h\" outgoing (h_n^(1)); wavenumber k. *)
psiScalar[n_, m_, k_, t_, c_, r_] :=
  Module[{rel = r - c, rr},
   rr = Sqrt[rel . rel];
   zfn[n, k rr, t] Yfun[n, m, rel]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5325f0fd-99b7-4051-b74e-23e13e9aefcc"],

Cell["\<\
SCALAR SEPARATION MATRIX  beta^c_{nm, nu mu}(d)   (closed form: \
Gegenbauer/Gaunt)
   Defined by:  h_n(k|r-a|) Y_n^m(^(r-a)) = Sum_{nu mu} beta[n,m,nu,mu,d,k]
                                            j_nu(k|r-b|) Y_nu^mu(^(r-b)),
   with d = a - b and valid for |r-b| < |d|.\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a405511a-e606-4fb3-abac-457df7e091fb"],

Cell["\<\
(* Gaunt integral  G(l1,m1;l2,m2;l3,m3) = Integral Y_l1^m1 Y_l2^m2 Y_l3^m3 \
dOmega *)
gaunt[l1_, m1_, l2_, m2_, l3_, m3_] :=
  If[m1 + m2 + m3 != 0 || Abs[m1] > l1 || Abs[m2] > l2 || Abs[m3] > l3, 0,
   Sqrt[(2 l1 + 1) (2 l2 + 1) (2 l3 + 1)/(4 Pi)]
     ThreeJSymbol[{l1, 0}, {l2, 0}, {l3, 0}] ThreeJSymbol[{l1, m1}, {l2, m2}, \
{l3, m3}]];

(* Closed-form singular->regular separation matrix (Rayleigh/Gegenbauer route).
   Derived: beta_{00,nu mu} = sqrt(4Pi) h_nu(kd) conj(Y_nu^mu(^d)), \
generalised via Gaunt.
   The q-sum is automatically parity-restricted by the {l,0} 3j (n+nu+q \
even). *)
betaSep[n_, m_, nu_, mu_, dvec_, k_] :=
  Module[{dl = Sqrt[dvec . dvec]},
   4 Pi (-1)^m Sum[
     I^(nu + q - n) (-1)^q sh[q, k dl] Yfun[q, m - mu, dvec] gaunt[n, m, nu, \
-mu, q, mu - m],
     {q, Abs[n - nu], n + nu}]];

(* Independent ground-truth coefficient by spherical-harmonic projection on a \
sphere
   of radius rho < |d| about B (origin); exact and phase-unambiguous, beta \
indep. of rho.
   Deterministic Gauss-Legendre(u=cos th) x uniform-phi quadrature: \
spectrally accurate
   for the smooth shifted-multipole integrand, no adaptive-NIntegrate \
fragility. *)
Needs[\"NumericalDifferentialEquationAnalysis`\"];
glNodes = GaussianQuadratureWeights[48, -1, 1];   (* {{u_i, w_i}} over \
cos(theta) in [-1,1] *)
nPhiQuad = 96;
betaProj[n_, m_, nu_, mu_, dvec_, k_, rho_] :=
  Module[{acc = 0., u, w, th, ph, shat},
   Do[
    u = glNodes[[i, 1]]; w = glNodes[[i, 2]]; th = ArcCos[u];
    Do[
     ph = 2 Pi (j - 1)/nPhiQuad;
     shat = {Sin[th] Cos[ph], Sin[th] Sin[ph], u};
     acc += w (2 Pi/nPhiQuad)
        psiScalar[n, m, k, \"h\", dvec, rho shat] \
Conjugate[SphericalHarmonicY[nu, mu, th, ph]],
     {j, nPhiQuad}],
    {i, Length[glNodes]}];
   acc/sj[nu, k rho]];

(* ---- reconstruction residual: max over sources (n,m) and field points ---- \
*)
(* a = b + dvec; we put B at the origin, A at dvec.  betaFn supplies the \
coeffs. *)
scalarReconResidual[betaFn_, k_, dvec_, NmaxNu_, sources_, fieldPts_] :=
  Module[{bcen = {0, 0, 0}, acen = dvec, lhs, rhs},
   Max[Table[
     lhs = psiScalar[src[[1]], src[[2]], k, \"h\", acen, pt];
     rhs = Sum[
        betaFn[src[[1]], src[[2]], nu, mu, dvec, k]
          psiScalar[nu, mu, k, \"j\", bcen, pt],
        {nu, 0, NmaxNu}, {mu, -nu, nu}];
     Abs[lhs - rhs],
     {src, sources}, {pt, fieldPts}]]];

(* ---- test fixture ---- *)
kTest = 0.9;                                  (* P-wavenumber test value (a=1 \
units) *)
dTest = {1.3, 0.7, 0.0};                      (* horizontal separation, Delta \
z = 0 *)
dLen = Sqrt[dTest . dTest];                   (* ~1.476, k*d ~ 1.33 *)
NmaxNuTest = 18;                              (* truncation of the regular \
re-expansion *)
sourcesTest = Flatten[Table[{n, m}, {n, 0, 3}, {m, -n, n}], 1];

(* deterministic cloud of field points near B, with |r-B| = rho < |d| (rho/d \
= 0.3) *)
SeedRandom[20260618];
rhoTest = 0.20 dLen;
fieldPtsTest = Table[
   Module[{u = RandomReal[{-1, 1}], ph = RandomReal[{0, 2 Pi}], st},
    st = Sqrt[1 - u^2];
    rhoTest {st Cos[ph], st Sin[ph], u}],
   {15}];

Print[\"==== Phase 0 :: SCALAR addition theorem ====\"];
Print[\"  k*d = \", kTest dLen, \",  rho/d = \", rhoTest/dLen,
   \",  Nmax(nu) = \", NmaxNuTest, \",  #sources = \", Length[sourcesTest],
   \",  #fieldpts = \", Length[fieldPtsTest]];

(* (a) closed form vs independent projection-integral ground truth *)
tolScalar = 1*^-7;
coefTests = {{0, 0, 2, 1}, {1, -1, 3, 2}, {2, 0, 2, -1}, {3, 1, 1, 0}, {2, 2, \
4, -2}, {1, 1, 5, 3}};
coefDiff = Max[Table[
    Abs[betaSep[t[[1]], t[[2]], t[[3]], t[[4]], dTest, kTest]
        - betaProj[t[[1]], t[[2]], t[[3]], t[[4]], dTest, kTest, 0.3 dLen]],
    {t, coefTests}]];
Print[\"  [a] max |betaSep(closed) - betaProj(integral)| over \", \
Length[coefTests],
   \" indices = \", coefDiff, \"  -> \", If[coefDiff < tolScalar, \"PASS\", \
\"FAIL\"]];

(* (b) full field reconstruction over the point cloud *)
resScalar = scalarReconResidual[betaSep, kTest, dTest, NmaxNuTest, \
sourcesTest, fieldPtsTest];
Print[\"  [b] field reconstruction residual (max over \", \
Length[sourcesTest], \" sources x \",
   Length[fieldPtsTest], \" pts) = \", resScalar, \"  -> \", If[resScalar < \
tolScalar, \"PASS\", \"FAIL\"]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b59cdb00-e85c-46fe-bbdd-e5100a0c5171"],

Cell["\<\
VECTOR elastic translation.  Plain Hansen multipoles:
     Lw = (1/k_P) grad psiP        (P-wave; L-block decouples)
     Mw = curl((r-c) psiS)         (S-wave toroidal)
     Nw = (1/k_S) curl Mw          (S-wave poloidal)
   Operators commute with translation, so applying them to the scalar \
addition
   theorem gives (derived):
     Lw^A_nm = Sum_{nu mu} beta^P_{nm,nu mu}(d) Lw^B_{nu mu}
     Mw^A_nm = Sum_{nu mu} beta^S_{nm,nu mu}(d) [ Mw^B_{nu mu} - (grad \
psiS^B_{nu mu}) x d ]
     Nw^A_nm = Sum_{nu mu} beta^S_{nm,nu mu}(d) [ Nw^B_{nu mu} - (1/k_S) \
curl((grad psiS^B) x d) ]
   with curl((grad psi) x d) = (d.grad) grad psi + k_S^2 psi d   (d \
constant).
   The naive scalar-style M translation (NO cross-term) must FAIL: that is \
the RED
   that proves the vector cross-term is physically necessary.\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bf629789-9da5-4d1a-820c-c54583ec97a3"],

Cell["\<\
kPval = 0.9; kSval = 1.5;

(* d/dx of spherical Bessel / Hankel (from CartesianT0.wl) *)
zfp[n_, x_, \"j\"] := n/x sj[n, x] - sj[n + 1, x];
zfp[n_, x_, \"h\"] := n/x sh[n, x] - sh[n + 1, x];

(* vector spherical harmonics on a direction (from CartesianT0.wl); the \
symbolic
   theta-derivative of Y is memoised per (n,m) so the multipole sweep stays \
fast. *)
RMrot[t_, p_] := {{Sin[t] Cos[p], Cos[t] Cos[p], -Sin[p]},
   {Sin[t] Sin[p], Cos[t] Sin[p], Cos[p]}, {Cos[t], -Sin[t], 0}};
dthY[n_, m_] := dthY[n, m] = Module[{tt, pp, ex},
   ex = D[SphericalHarmonicY[n, m, tt, pp], tt]; Function[{a, b}, Evaluate[ex \
/. {tt -> a, pp -> b}]]];
Bvec[n_, m_, d_] := Module[{t = ang[d][[1]], p = ang[d][[2]]},
   RMrot[t, p] . {0, dthY[n, m][t, p], (I m/Sin[t]) SphericalHarmonicY[n, m, \
t, p]}];
Cvec[n_, m_, d_] := Cross[d/Sqrt[d . d], Bvec[n, m, d]];

(* field-point helpers *)
rhoOf[c_, r_] := Sqrt[(r - c) . (r - c)];
rhatOf[c_, r_] := (r - c)/Sqrt[(r - c) . (r - c)];

(* grad of the scalar multipole psi = z_n(k|r-c|) Y_n^m, centred at c *)
gradPsi[n_, m_, k_, type_, c_, r_] := Module[{rho = rhoOf[c, r]},
   k zfp[n, k rho, type] Yfun[n, m, r - c] rhatOf[c, r] + (zfn[n, k rho, \
type]/rho) Bvec[n, m, r - c]];

Lw[n_, m_, type_, c_, r_] := Module[{x = kPval rhoOf[c, r]},
   zfp[n, x, type] Yfun[n, m, r - c] rhatOf[c, r] + (zfn[n, x, type]/x) \
Bvec[n, m, r - c]];
Mw[n_, m_, type_, c_, r_] := -zfn[n, kSval rhoOf[c, r], type] Cvec[n, m, r - \
c];
Nw[n_, m_, type_, c_, r_] := Module[{x = kSval rhoOf[c, r]},
   (n (n + 1)/x) zfn[n, x, type] Yfun[n, m, r - c] rhatOf[c, r]
     + ((zfn[n, x, type] + x zfp[n, x, type])/x) Bvec[n, m, r - c]];

(* ---- reconstruction (B at origin, A at d); beta tables memoised per source \
---- *)
bcen0 = {0, 0, 0}; acen0 = dTest; dvec0 = dTest; epsFD = 1.*^-5; tolVec = \
1*^-6;
coefsP[n_, m_] := coefsP[n, m] =
   Flatten[Table[{nu, mu, betaSep[n, m, nu, mu, dvec0, kPval]}, {nu, 0, \
NmaxNuTest}, {mu, -nu, nu}], 1];
(* nu starts at 0: the monopole's scalar term feeds M,N through the \
cross-term
   (grad psiS_{00}) x d even though Mw_{00}=Nw_{00}=0. *)
coefsS[n_, m_] := coefsS[n, m] =
   Flatten[Table[{nu, mu, betaSep[n, m, nu, mu, dvec0, kSval]}, {nu, 0, \
NmaxNuTest}, {mu, -nu, nu}], 1];

reconL[n_, m_, r_] := Sum[c[[3]] Lw[c[[1]], c[[2]], \"j\", bcen0, r], {c, \
coefsP[n, m]}];
reconMnaive[n_, m_, r_] := Sum[c[[3]] Mw[c[[1]], c[[2]], \"j\", bcen0, r], \
{c, coefsS[n, m]}];
reconMfull[n_, m_, r_] := Sum[
   c[[3]] (Mw[c[[1]], c[[2]], \"j\", bcen0, r] - Cross[gradPsi[c[[1]], \
c[[2]], kSval, \"j\", bcen0, r], dvec0]),
   {c, coefsS[n, m]}];
dPsiDirD[nu_, mu_, r_] :=
   (gradPsi[nu, mu, kSval, \"j\", bcen0, r + epsFD dvec0] - gradPsi[nu, mu, \
kSval, \"j\", bcen0, r - epsFD dvec0])/(2 epsFD);
Ncross[nu_, mu_, r_] := (1/kSval) (dPsiDirD[nu, mu, r] + kSval^2 \
psiScalar[nu, mu, kSval, \"j\", bcen0, r] dvec0);
reconNfull[n_, m_, r_] := Sum[
   c[[3]] (Nw[c[[1]], c[[2]], \"j\", bcen0, r] - Ncross[c[[1]], c[[2]], r]), \
{c, coefsS[n, m]}];

vSrcL = Flatten[Table[{n, m}, {n, 0, 3}, {m, -n, n}], 1];
vSrcMN = Flatten[Table[{n, m}, {n, 1, 3}, {m, -n, n}], 1];
vFieldPts = Take[fieldPtsTest, 6];
vmax[lhs_, rhs_, srcs_] := Max[Table[Norm[lhs[s[[1]], s[[2]], pt] - \
rhs[s[[1]], s[[2]], pt]], {s, srcs}, {pt, vFieldPts}]];

(* internal consistency: confirm Mw = curl((r)psiS) and Nw = (1/k_S) curl Mw \
(finite diff) *)
curlFD[F_, r_, h_] := Module[{e1 = {1, 0, 0}, e2 = {0, 1, 0}, e3 = {0, 0, 1}, \
dd},
   dd[j_] := (F[r + h j] - F[r - h j])/(2 h);
   {dd[e2][[3]] - dd[e3][[2]], dd[e3][[1]] - dd[e1][[3]], dd[e1][[2]] - \
dd[e2][[1]]}];
rChk = {0.31, 0.22, 0.18};
selfChkSrc = {{1, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, -1}, {2, 2}, {3, 1}};
chkM = Max[Table[Norm[Mw[s[[1]], s[[2]], \"j\", {0, 0, 0}, rChk]
      - curlFD[(# psiScalar[s[[1]], s[[2]], kSval, \"j\", {0, 0, 0}, #]) &, \
rChk, 1.*^-5]], {s, selfChkSrc}]];
chkN = Max[Table[Norm[Nw[s[[1]], s[[2]], \"j\", {0, 0, 0}, rChk]
      - (1/kSval) curlFD[Mw[s[[1]], s[[2]], \"j\", {0, 0, 0}, #] &, rChk, \
1.*^-5]], {s, selfChkSrc}]];
Print[\"==== Phase 0 :: VECTOR field-definition self-check (finite diff) ====\
\"];
Print[\"  max |Mw - curl((r) psiS)|      = \", chkM, \"  -> \", If[chkM < \
1*^-5, \"PASS\", \"FAIL\"]];
Print[\"  max |Nw - (1/k_S) curl Mw|     = \", chkN, \"  -> \", If[chkN < \
1*^-5, \"PASS\", \"FAIL\"]];

Print[\"==== Phase 0 :: VECTOR elastic translation  (k_P=\", kPval, \", \
k_S=\", kSval, \") ====\"];
resVL = vmax[Lw[#1, #2, \"h\", acen0, #3] &, reconL, vSrcL];
Print[\"  L (P-wave) recon, beta^P  [criterion iii: L = scalar]   = \", \
resVL,
   \"  -> \", If[resVL < tolVec, \"PASS\", \"FAIL\"]];
resVMn = vmax[Mw[#1, #2, \"h\", acen0, #3] &, reconMnaive, vSrcMN];
Print[\"  M (S toroidal) recon, NAIVE beta^S only (no cross-term) = \", resVMn,
   \"  -> \", If[resVMn < tolVec, \"PASS\", \"FAIL (expected: cross-term \
needed)\"]];
resVMf = vmax[Mw[#1, #2, \"h\", acen0, #3] &, reconMfull, vSrcMN];
Print[\"  M (S toroidal) recon, FULL (beta^S + (grad psi) x d)    = \", resVMf,
   \"  -> \", If[resVMf < tolVec, \"PASS\", \"FAIL\"]];
resVNf = vmax[Nw[#1, #2, \"h\", acen0, #3] &, reconNfull, vSrcMN];
Print[\"  N (S poloidal) recon, FULL (beta^S + curl cross-term)   = \", resVNf,
   \"  -> \", If[resVNf < tolVec, \"PASS\", \"FAIL\"]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c97aabed-1cff-440c-8504-e698a06e68c2"],

Cell["\<\
RECIPROCITY of the translation operator (closed-form symmetry, derived from
   the Gaunt form; the per-term i^(nu+q-n)/i^(n+q-nu) ratio collapses to \
(-1)^(nu-n)):
     beta_{nm,nu mu}(d) = (-1)^(n+nu+m+mu) beta_{nu,-mu, n,-m}(d).
   Verified analytically against the n=0 row; here checked numerically.\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"add1dfb4-aeb1-401b-8ea3-6589f811f0cc"],

Cell["\<\
recipPairs = {{1, 0, 2, 1}, {2, -1, 3, 2}, {3, 1, 1, -1}, {2, 2, 4, -2}, {0, \
0, 3, 0}, {1, 1, 2, -2}};
recipResid[k_] := Max[Table[
    Abs[betaSep[p[[1]], p[[2]], p[[3]], p[[4]], dTest, k]
       - (-1)^(p[[1]] + p[[3]] + p[[2]] + p[[4]]) betaSep[p[[3]], -p[[4]], \
p[[1]], -p[[2]], dTest, k]],
    {p, recipPairs}]];
tolRecip = 1*^-11;
Print[\"==== Phase 0 :: RECIPROCITY (translation-operator symmetry) ====\"];
Print[\"  max |beta_{nm,nu mu}(d) - (-1)^(n+nu+m+mu) beta_{nu,-mu,n,-m}(d)|,  \
k_P = \",
   recipResid[kPval], \"  -> \", If[recipResid[kPval] < tolRecip, \"PASS\", \
\"FAIL\"]];
Print[\"  same at k_S = \", recipResid[kSval], \"  -> \", \
If[recipResid[kSval] < tolRecip, \"PASS\", \"FAIL\"]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d344625e-f9b8-457f-9436-e4b1e6a65efa"],

Cell["\<\
Dump closed-form beta to JSON for the INDEPENDENT Python cross-check
   (Python recomputes beta by spherical-harmonic projection: different \
method,
   different language).  Mirrors the ElasticMie_reference.json pattern.\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6265896b-11f5-4586-8a84-b0399b498459"],

Cell["\<\
mkDump[k_] := Flatten[Table[
    <|\"n\" -> n, \"m\" -> m, \"nu\" -> nu, \"mu\" -> mu,
      \"re\" -> Re[N[betaSep[n, m, nu, mu, dTest, k]]],
      \"im\" -> Im[N[betaSep[n, m, nu, mu, dTest, k]]]|>,
    {n, 0, 3}, {m, -n, n}, {nu, 0, 3}, {mu, -nu, nu}], 3];
refData = <|\"dvec\" -> dTest, \"kP\" -> kPval, \"kS\" -> kSval,
   \"betaP\" -> mkDump[kPval], \"betaS\" -> mkDump[kSval]|>;
Export[\"/Users/tod/Desktop/MultipleScatteringCalculations/Mathematica/\
IntraPlaneTranslation_reference.json\",
   refData];
Print[\"==== Phase 0 :: reference dump ====\"];
Print[\"  wrote IntraPlaneTranslation_reference.json: \",
   Length[refData[\"betaP\"]], \" betaP + \", Length[refData[\"betaS\"]], \" \
betaS entries\"];
Print[\"Phase 0 (IntraPlaneTranslation.wl) loaded + verified.\"];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4e30eb59-8f5f-4159-a009-1620f2682019"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"14.3 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 8, 2025)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"8f6fdcca-0c61-4c6c-802d-75c69cfc4bd0"
]
